    "id": "refurbished-is-a-question-not-a-verdict",
    "title": "When refurbished medical equipment is the better buy",
    "summary": "Judge a refurbished candidate by its documented work, complete configuration, acceptance terms and support at the destination.",
    "intro": "Refurbished equipment is worth buying when the lower complete cost preserves the capability and support the hospital needs. It is a weaker offer when the saving depends on missing accessories, uncertain software rights or a repair route that stops at the seller’s border. Compare the particular unit with a suitable new option and with repairing what the hospital already owns.",
    "sections": [
      [
        "Ask what happened to this unit",
        "Request the work completed, by whom, when and against which procedure, supported by actual-unit photographs and available service records. Cleaning, inspection, battery replacement and a documented functional assessment describe different work. Ask the supplier to explain its condition terminology for this unit. Where records are incomplete, identify what a qualified independent assessment can establish and price it before committing. Missing paperwork is a reason to investigate specific uncertainty; it is not evidence that the unit either works well or is unusable."
      ],
      [
        "Look for a coherent configuration",
        "An older unit may have accumulated replacement components or software changes. List the current hardware, accessories and licensed functions and ask qualified reviewers to confirm that they form a supported configuration. For a monitor, this means the measurement modules and sensors, not only the display. Philips’ modular monitoring documentation provides a concrete example of how measurement capability sits in components that must be identified. A model name is too broad a description for the purchase order."
      ],
      [
        "Check support in the place it will be used",
        "A device that is serviceable in one country may be difficult to support in another. Ask who will provide local technical work, where parts come from and which software or documentation the service provider can legitimately access. Find out whether the manufacturer supports that generation and obtain the applicable instructions. Review relevant manufacturer notices and regulator recall information for the model and affected serial range. A database search is a useful input, not a certificate that an individual unit has no unresolved issue."
      ],
      [
        "Make acceptance part of the bargain",
        "Before payment and shipment, agree the condition and configuration evidence, the qualified reviewers and the remedy if the package differs. Include missing accessories and freight damage. Dispatch checks establish what leaves the seller; installed acceptance addresses the equipment after transport and any site-dependent work. Record which costs fall to each party, when the warranty starts and what must happen before the receiving team accepts the unit. A price reduction has little value if it comes with an unresolved essential defect."
      ],
      [
        "Proceed, investigate or choose another route",
        "Proceed when the candidate meets the clinical brief, its condition is evidenced, support is workable and its complete cost compares well. Investigate when a defined assessment can settle a material uncertainty before commitment. Choose another route when essential compatibility, software transfer, parts access or acceptance rights cannot be established.\n\nA supported familiar platform can be attractive where the hospital already has compatible accessories, trained users and a credible engineer. Count only items confirmed suitable for the offered generation. A new platform may deserve the premium when it provides a needed function or resolves the old fleet’s support limit. Repairing the existing unit remains a third option if its fault is understood and the restored service meets the same brief. Compare future spending; past repair bills are useful history, not a reason to keep paying indefinitely."
      ]
    ],
    "checklist": [
      "Ask for unit-specific condition and work records",
      "Identify the complete supported configuration",
      "Confirm local parts and service access",
      "Agree acceptance criteria before shipment"
    ],
